// From the law, paragraph 41 of the Instructions of 2025, with the width as 20:
//   length to width 3:2; white 1/4 at the mast (7.5), the rest dark green
//   A is the center of the green portion, at fly 18.75, hoist 10
//   the diagonal runs from the green's lower hoist to its top fly corner, length 30.10399
//   B is on it, 13/20 of the width (13) from that corner, so 2.05199 from A
//   inner arc: radius "1.1/4th" of the width = 5.5
//   star in a circle "1/10th" of the width, read as radius 2, one point on the diagonal
//     where the outer arc cuts it. So its center is 6 - 2 = 4 from A, at 21.73964, 7.34254
// From elsewhere: the law's text drops the outer arc, and gives the 5.5 to A. Radius 6
// around A and 5.5 around B are from FOTW's account of the Interior Ministry's figures.
// Rotations are the diagonal's angle, derived here. The hex is from Wikipedia, via FOTW.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Pakistan"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "Apache-2.0"
  source "https://balochistancode.gob.pk/pdfviewer.aspx?pdffile=37fcba70-1655-488d-9ac1-1718a978b3ca.pdf"
  source "https://www.crwflags.com/fotw/flags/pk'.html"
  source "https://www.crwflags.com/fotw/flags/pk.html"
  source "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag_of_Pakistan"
  note "The gazetted description omits the outer arc and gives the inner arc's radius with center A. The outer radius of 3/10 of the width and the reading of the inner arc as centered on B come from FOTW's contributors, working from the Interior Ministry's figures and Pakistan Standard 1700 of 1985, which wasn't read. The star's circle of 1/10 of the width is read as a radius, following those same figures."
  note "The law gives only Pantone codes, 19-5917 and 12-4306, as TPX for paper and TCX for fabric. No published conversion of them was read. The green's hex is the one FOTW reports from Wikipedia, and Wikipedia names the shade as 19-5917 TCX. The Album des Pavillons 2023 gives Pantone 342 C, RGB 0-106-78, instead, a lighter green than the law's code suggests."
  note "White is drawn as plain white, because no conversion of the law's code 12-4306 was read."
  law "Instructions on the Design and Use of the Pakistan Flag and Use of Flags of Foreign Countries in Pakistan, Cabinet Division notification of 20 October 2025, paragraphs 41 to 43" {
    source "https://balochistancode.gob.pk/pdfviewer.aspx?pdffile=37fcba70-1655-488d-9ac1-1718a978b3ca.pdf"
  }
  law "Resolution of the Constituent Assembly of Pakistan on the National Flag of the Federation of Pakistan, 11 August 1947" {
    source "https://balochistancode.gob.pk/pdfviewer.aspx?pdffile=37fcba70-1655-488d-9ac1-1718a978b3ca.pdf"
  }
}
palette {
  white "#ffffff" {
    pantone "12-4306 TPX"
    reference "Pantone, for fabric" "12-4306 TCX"
  }
  green "#01411c" {
    pantone "19-5917 TPX"
    reference "Pantone, for fabric" "19-5917 TCX"
  }
}
proportion hoist=20 fly=30

bars white green {
  along hoist
  ratio 1 3
}
charge crescent white {
  radius 6
  inner 5.5
  offset 2.05199
  rotate -41.63354
  at fly=18.75 hoist=10
}
charge star white {
  radius 2
  rotate 48.36646
  at fly=21.73964 hoist=7.34254
}
